/* book Worked example: Q: A three-phase fully controlled bridge is fed from a 400 V, 50 Hz line, with continuous load current, at α = 30°. Find (a) Vdc, (b) the lowest ripple frequency and (c) Vdc of a three-pulse circuit on the same supply at the same α.
   1. (a) Vd0 = 3√2 × 400/π = 1697.06/3.1416 = 540.19 V. Vdc = 540.19 × cos 30° = 540.19 × 0.8660 = 467.82 V.
   2. (b) p = 6, so the lowest ripple frequency is 6 × 50 = 300 Hz.
   3. (c) Vph = 400/√3 = 230.94 V and Vm = √2 × 230.94 = 326.60 V. Vdc = (3√3 × 326.60/2π) × 0.8660 = 270.09 × 0.8660 = 233.91 V, exactly half the bridge value.
   Answer: (a) 467.8 V; (b) 300 Hz; (c) 233.9 V. */
