/* book Worked example 2: Q: The same bridge feeds a pure 10 Ω resistance at α = 75°. Find Vdc and Id, and compare with the continuous-current formula.
   1. α = 75° is above 60°, so with R the current is discontinuous.
   2. Vdc = 540.19 × [1 + cos(75° + 60°)] = 540.19 × (1 − 0.7071) = 540.19 × 0.2929 = 158.22 V.
   3. Id = 158.22/10 = 15.82 A.
   4. The cosine formula gives 540.19 × cos 75° = 540.19 × 0.2588 = 139.81 V, 18.4 V too low: it counts negative slices that a resistive load cannot produce.
   Answer: Vdc = 158.2 V and Id = 15.8 A; the continuous-current formula would wrongly give 139.8 V. */
