/* book exam traps: Measuring α in a three-phase circuit from the zero crossing of the phase voltage. It is measured from the crossing of two phase voltages, 30° later. | Putting phase voltage into 1.35 VL cos α or line voltage into 1.17 Vph cos α. | Saying each thyristor of the bridge conducts for 60°. Each conducts 120°; a new pair forms every 60°. | Using 1.35 VL cos α for an R load above α = 60°. The output is then (3√2 VL/π)[1 + cos(α + 60°)], higher than the cosine value. | Expecting a neutral connection for the six-pulse bridge. Only the three-pulse circuit needs one. */
