/* book Worked example: Q: A single-phase fully controlled bridge on 230 V, 50 Hz carries a level load current Id = 10 A at α = 30°. Find I1, g, THD, DF, PF, the real and reactive input power, and check the power against the DC side.
   1. I1 = (2√2/π) × 10 = 0.9003 × 10 = 9.00 A; Is = Id = 10 A; g = 9.00/10 = 0.900.
   2. THD = √(1/0.9003² − 1) = √(1.2337 − 1) = 0.483, that is 48.3 %.
   3. DF = cos 30° = 0.866; PF = 0.900 × 0.866 = 0.780.
   4. P = Vs I1 cos φ1 = 230 × 9.003 × 0.866 = 1793 W; S = Vs Is = 230 × 10 = 2300 VA; P/S = 0.780, as above.
   5. Q1 = Vs I1 sin φ1 = 230 × 9.003 × 0.5 = 1035 var.
   6. DC side: Vdc = 207.07 × 0.866 = 179.33 V, so Vdc Id = 1793 W, equal to P, as it must be for an ideal converter.
   Answer: I1 = 9.00 A, g = 0.900, THD = 48.3 %, DF = 0.866, PF = 0.780, P = 1793 W, Q1 = 1035 var. */
