/* book Worked example 2: Q: The three-phase bridge of the earlier example (400 V, α = 30°, Vdc = 467.82 V) carries Id = 50 A. Find the line RMS current, I1, PF, THD and the 5th and 7th harmonic currents.
   1. Is = √(2/3) × 50 = 40.82 A; I1 = (√6/π) × 50 = 38.98 A; g = 38.98/40.82 = 0.955.
   2. PF = g cos α = 0.955 × 0.866 = 0.827. Check: P = 467.82 × 50 = 23.39 kW, S = √3 × 400 × 40.82 = 28.28 kVA, P/S = 0.827.
   3. THD = √(1/0.955² − 1) = 0.311, that is 31.1 %.
   4. I5 = I1/5 = 7.80 A and I7 = I1/7 = 5.57 A; there is no 3rd harmonic.
   Answer: Is = 40.82 A, I1 = 38.98 A, PF = 0.827, THD = 31.1 %, I5 = 7.80 A, I7 = 5.57 A. */
