/* book exam traps: Writing PF = cos α. That is only the displacement factor; the distortion factor (0.900 or 0.955) multiplies it. | Listing even harmonics or a 3rd harmonic for a three-phase bridge. Half-wave symmetry removes the even ones, and the 120° blocks remove the triplens: only 6k ± 1 remain. | Computing RF from Vpeak − Vdc. RF uses the RMS of the ripple: √(FF² − 1). | Subtracting THD from 1 to get g. They are linked by g = 1/√(1 + THD²). | Mixing up DF: in some books it is the displacement factor, in others the distortion factor. State the definition you use. */
